        <p class="section-kicker">Demand Planning & Visibility</p>
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-3">Forecasting & Supply Network Intelligence</h2>
        <p>
            Demand planning uses historical consumption patterns, seasonal factors, and growth
            projections to forecast material requirements. Safety stock levels optimize the balance
            between service levels and working capital — ensuring availability without excessive
            inventory carrying costs.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-0">
            End-to-end visibility connects supplier lead times, in-transit inventory, warehouse
            stock levels, and customer demand signals into a unified view. Exception-based management
            highlights supply risks, delayed shipments, and potential stockouts before they impact
            downstream operations or customer commitments.
        </p>
    </div>
